From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 22:03:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sidebar): never auto-group internal or temporary
 workspaces [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Use one realpath/normcase policy for git roots, session cwds and cached
repo discovery. Internal/temp sessions go to Home even when a linked
worktree resolves to an external common repo. Explicit user projects stay
honored. Normalize copied tree inputs/resolver results before ownership
and lane grouping, so symlink spellings do not create duplicate lanes.
Include sibling profile homes, including externally symlinked profiles.

Five whys:
1. The reported desktop chat had cwd ~/.hermes/cache/scratch.noindex and
   recent activity, so it appeared under a scratch.noindex auto group.
2. Tier 2 promoted every non-git cwd not rejected by is_junk_cwd.
3. _is_session_cwd_junk excluded only HERMES_HOME itself, while
   _is_repo_junk excluded descendants: inconsistent policy.
4. Darwin ensure_spotlight_noindex_dir makes scratch a symlink to
   scratch.noindex. A real-symlink fixture confirms that the old grouping
   can split both spellings into distinct lanes/projects.
5. There was no single never-a-workspace policy. Existing coverage omitted
   home descendants, profile scratch, worktrees and OS temp roots.
Related recurrence: deleted-workspace phantoms and private
subagent scratch cwds. No sweeping or archiving is introduced.

Proof:
- RED on main 106bf5b0b97f2e3748767e2a46b6cc3e40a1f9f5:
  bash scripts/run_tests.sh tests/tui_gateway/test_project_non_workspace.py
  => 11 failed, 1 passed (expected auto-project/alias assertions).
- Additional sibling-profile symlink boundary RED: 1 failed, 14 passed
  before profile-target enumeration.
- GREEN (HERMES_TEST_FILE_RETRIES=0): project non-workspace/tree/RPC,
  profiles_sidebar_scope, projects_tree_prewarm, session_surface_lists,
  subagent_session_activity, gui_sidebar_provenance: 127 passed, 0 failed.
- Desktop placement/nested/overview sidebar oracle suites: 106 passed,
  3 files, Node 26.12.1, isolated lockfile-installed dependency worktree.
- scripts/hermes-python scripts/check --base origin/main: 21 checks pass.
- Read-only laptop cwd inventory: most distinct cwds newly classify as
  internal (mostly Hermes-owned, a few temp), across all stored sessions. This is
  a classifier inventory, not a count of visible sidebar changes.

Secondary attribution investigation:
The supposed dormant-chat/wrong-parent premise is refuted. Active
message_count omits retained history: read-only laptop inspection found
tens of thousands of message rows in the reported parent, including its own
earlier assistant delegate_task calls (independently checked). Investigation
matched every child's goal to that parent's persisted spawn calls, with child
creation seconds later. Parent is passed explicitly by run_agent into delegate_task, not
selected from inherited HERMES_SESSION_ID on this path. No attribution
repair, archive, or producer rewrite is justified for these rows.

Deployment acceptance remains on the owning card: canonical ship,
independent exact-head review, exact-head CI, and post-deploy laptop
projects/tree readback showing no scratch/internal/temp auto group.

